@.str.3 = private unnamed_addr constant [62172 x i8] c"Additional cvc5 options:\0A\0AFrom the Arithmetic Theory module:\0A  --approx-branch-depth=N\0A                         maximum branch depth the approximate solver is allowed\0A                         to take (EXPERTS only)\0A  --arith-brab           whether to use simple rounding, similar to a unit-cube\0A                         test, for integers [*]\0A  --arith-eq-solver      whether to use the equality solver in the theory of\0A                         arithmetic (EXPERTS only) [*]\0A  --arith-exp            enables non-standard extensions of the arithmetic\0A                         solver (EXPERTS only) [*]\0A  --arith-prop=MODE      turns on arithmetic propagation (default is 'old', see\0A                         --arith-prop=help) (EXPERTS only)\0A  --arith-prop-clauses=N rows shorter than this are propagated as clauses\0A                         (EXPERTS only)\0A  --arith-rewrite-equalities\0A                         turns on the preprocessing rewrite turning equalities\0A                         into a conjunction of inequalities [*]\0A  --arith-static-learning\0A                         do arithmetic static learning for ite terms based on\0A                         bounds when static learning is enabled [*]\0A  --collect-pivot-stats  collect the pivot history (EXPERTS only) [*]\0A  --cut-all-bounded      turns on the integer solving step of periodically\0A                         cutting all integer variables that have both upper and\0A                         lower bounds (EXPERTS only) [*]\0A  --dio-decomps          let skolem variables for integer divisibility\0A                         constraints leak from the dio solver (EXPERTS only) [*]\0A  --dio-solver           turns on Linear Diophantine Equation solver (Griggio,\0A                         JSAT 2012) (EXPERTS only) [*]\0A  --dio-turns=N          turns in a row dio solver cutting gets (EXPERTS only)\0A  --error-selection-rule=RULE\0A                         change the pivot rule for the basic variable (default\0A                         is 'min', see --pivot-rule help) (EXPERTS only)\0A  --fc-penalties         turns on degenerate pivot penalties (EXPERTS only) [*]\0A  --heuristic-pivots=N   the number of times to apply the heuristic pivot rule;\0A                         if N < 0, this defaults to the number of variables; if\0A                         this is unset, this is tuned by the logic selection\0A                         (EXPERTS only)\0A  --lemmas-on-replay-failure\0A                         attempt to use external lemmas if approximate solve\0A                         integer failed (EXPERTS only) [*]\0A  --maxCutsInContext=N   maximum cuts in a given context before signalling a\0A                         restart (EXPERTS only)\0A  --miplib-trick         turns on the preprocessing step of attempting to infer\0A                         bounds on miplib problems (EXPERTS only) [*]\0A  --miplib-trick-subs=N  do substitution for miplib 'tmp' vars if defined in <=\0A                         N eliminated vars (EXPERTS only)\0A  --new-prop             use the new row propagation system (EXPERTS only) [*]\0A  --nl-cov               whether to use the cylindrical algebraic coverings\0A                         solver for non-linear arithmetic [*]\0A  --nl-cov-force         forces using the cylindrical algebraic coverings\0A                         solver, even in cases where it is possibly not safe to\0A                         do so (EXPERTS only) [*]\0A  --nl-cov-lift=MODE     choose the Coverings lifting mode (EXPERTS only)\0A  --nl-cov-linear-model=MODE\0A                         whether to use the linear model as initial guess for\0A                         the cylindrical algebraic coverings solver\0A  --nl-cov-proj=MODE     choose the Coverings projection operator (EXPERTS only)\0A  --nl-cov-prune         whether to prune intervals more aggressively (EXPERTS\0A                         only) [*]\0A  --nl-cov-var-elim      whether to eliminate variables using equalities before\0A                         going into the cylindrical algebraic coverings solver.\0A                         It can not be used when producing proofs right now.\0A                         (EXPERTS only) [*]\0A  --nl-ext=MODE          incremental linearization approach to non-linear\0A  --nl-ext-ent-conf      check for entailed conflicts in non-linear solver\0A                         (EXPERTS only) [*]\0A  --nl-ext-factor        use factoring inference in non-linear incremental\0A                         linearization solver [*]\0A  --nl-ext-inc-prec      whether to increment the precision for irrational\0A                         function constraints (EXPERTS only) [*]\0A  --nl-ext-purify        purify non-linear terms at preprocess (EXPERTS only)\0A                         [*]\0A  --nl-ext-rbound        use resolution-style inference for inferring new bounds\0A                         in non-linear incremental linearization solver (EXPERTS\0A                         only) [*]\0A  --nl-ext-rewrite       do context-dependent simplification based on rewrites\0A                         in non-linear solver [*]\0A  --nl-ext-split-zero    initial splits on zero for all variables (EXPERTS only)\0A                         [*]\0A  --nl-ext-tf-taylor-deg=N\0A                         initial degree of polynomials for Taylor approximation\0A                         (EXPERTS only)\0A  --nl-ext-tf-tplanes    use non-terminating tangent plane strategy for\0A                         transcendental functions for non-linear incremental\0A                         linearization solver [*]\0A  --nl-ext-tplanes       use non-terminating tangent plane strategy for\0A                         non-linear incremental linearization solver [*]\0A  --nl-ext-tplanes-interleave\0A                         interleave tangent plane strategy for non-linear\0A                         incremental linearization solver [*]\0A  --nl-icp               whether to use ICP-style propagations for non-linear\0A                         arithmetic (EXPERTS only) [*]\0A  --nl-rlv=MODE          choose mode for using relevance of assertions in\0A                         non-linear arithmetic (EXPERTS only)\0A  --nl-rlv-assert-bounds use bound inference utility to prune when an assertion\0A                         is entailed by another (EXPERTS only) [*]\0A  --pb-rewrites          apply pseudo boolean rewrites (EXPERTS only) [*]\0A  --pivot-threshold=N    sets the number of pivots using --pivot-rule per basic\0A                         variable per simplex instance before using variable\0A                         order (EXPERTS only)\0A  --pp-assert-max-sub-size=N\0A                         threshold for substituting an equality in ppAssert\0A                         (EXPERTS only)\0A  --prop-row-length=N    sets the maximum row length to be used in propagation\0A                         (EXPERTS only)\0A  --replay-early-close-depth=N\0A                         multiples of the depths to try to close the approx log\0A                         eagerly (EXPERTS only)\0A  --replay-lemma-reject-cut=N\0A                         maximum complexity of any coefficient while outputting\0A                         replaying cut lemmas (EXPERTS only)\0A  --replay-num-err-penalty=N\0A                         number of solve integer attempts to skips after a\0A                         numeric failure (EXPERTS only)\0A  --replay-reject-cut=N  maximum complexity of any coefficient while replaying\0A                         cuts (EXPERTS only)\0A  --restrict-pivots      have a pivot cap for simplex at effort levels below\0A                         fullEffort (EXPERTS only) [*]\0A  --revert-arith-models-on-unsat\0A                         revert the arithmetic model to a known safe model on\0A                         unsat if one is cached (EXPERTS only) [*]\0A  --rr-turns=N           round robin turn (EXPERTS only)\0A  --se-solve-int         attempt to use the approximate solve integer method on\0A                         standard effort (EXPERTS only) [*]\0A  --simplex-check-period=N\0A                         the number of pivots to do in simplex before rechecking\0A                         for a conflict on all variables (EXPERTS only)\0A  --soi-qe               use quick explain to minimize the sum of infeasibility\0A                         conflicts (EXPERTS only) [*]\0A  --standard-effort-variable-order-pivots=N\0A                         limits the number of pivots in a single invocation of\0A                         check() at a non-full effort level using Bland's pivot\0A                         rule (EXPERTS only)\0A  --unate-lemmas=MODE    determines which lemmas to add before solving (default\0A                         is 'all', see --unate-lemmas=help) (EXPERTS only)\0A  --use-approx           attempt to use an approximate solver (EXPERTS only) [*]\0A  --use-fcsimplex        use focusing and converging simplex (FMCAD 2013\0A                         submission) (EXPERTS only) [*]\0A  --use-soi              use sum of infeasibility simplex (FMCAD 2013\0A                         submission) (EXPERTS only) [*]\0A\0AFrom the Arrays Theory module:\0A  --arrays-eager-index   turn on eager index splitting for generated array\0A                         lemmas [*]\0A  --arrays-eager-lemmas  turn on eager lemma generation for arrays (EXPERTS\0A                         only) [*]\0A  --arrays-exp           enable experimental features in the theory of arrays\0A                         (EXPERTS only) [*]\0A  --arrays-optimize-linear\0A                         turn on optimization for linear array terms (see de\0A                         Moura FMCAD 09 arrays paper) (EXPERTS only) [*]\0A  --arrays-prop=N        propagation effort for arrays: 0 is none, 1 is some, 2\0A                         is full (EXPERTS only)\0A  --arrays-reduce-sharing\0A                         use model information to reduce size of care graph for\0A                         arrays (EXPERTS only) [*]\0A  --arrays-weak-equiv    use algorithm from Christ/Hoenicke (SMT 2014) (EXPERTS\0A                         only) [*]\0A\0AFrom the Bags Theory module:\0A  --bags                 enables the bags solver in applicable logics (EXPERTS\0A                         only) [*]\0A\0AFrom the Base module:\0A  --err=erroutput | --diagnostic-output-channel=erroutput\0A                         Set the error (or diagnostic) output channel. Writes to\0A                         stderr for \22stderr\22 or \22--\22, stdout for \22stdout\22 or the\0A                         given filename otherwise. (EXPERTS only)\0A  --in=input             Set the error (or diagnostic) output channel. Reads\0A                         from stdin for \22stdin\22 or \22--\22 and the given filename\0A                         otherwise. (EXPERTS only)\0A  --out=output | --regular-output-channel=output\0A                         Set the error (or diagnostic) output channel. Writes to\0A                         stdout for \22stdout\22 or \22--\22, stderr for \22stderr\22 or the\0A                         given filename otherwise. (EXPERTS only)\0A  --plugin-notify-sat-clause-in-solve\0A                         only inform plugins of SAT clauses when we are in the\0A                         main solving loop of the SAT solver (EXPERTS only) [*]\0A  --plugin-share-skolems true if we permit sharing theory lemmas and SAT clauses\0A                         with skolems (EXPERTS only) [*]\0A  --rweight=VAL=N        set a single resource weight (EXPERTS only)\0A  --safe-options         do not allow setting any option that is not common or\0A                         regular (EXPERTS only) [*]\0A  --stats-every-query    in incremental mode, print stats after every\0A                         satisfiability or validity query [*]\0A  --trace=TAG | -t TAG   trace something (e.g. -t pushpop), can repeat and may\0A                         contain wildcards like (e.g. -t theory::*)\0A\0AFrom the Bitvector Theory module:\0A  --bitblast=MODE        choose bitblasting mode, see --bitblast=help\0A  --bitwise-eq           lift equivalence with one-bit bit-vectors to be boolean\0A                         operations [*]\0A  --bool-to-bv=MODE      convert booleans to bit-vectors of size 1 at various\0A                         levels of aggressiveness, see --bool-to-bv=help\0A  --bv-assert-input      assert input assertions on user-level 0 instead of\0A                         assuming them in the bit-vector SAT solver (EXPERTS\0A                         only) [*]\0A  --bv-eager-eval        perform eager context-dependent evaluation for\0A                         applications of bv kinds in the equality engine [*]\0A  --bv-eq-engine         enable equality engine when possible in bitvector\0A                         theory (EXPERTS only) [*]\0A  --bv-gauss-elim        simplify formula via Gaussian Elimination if applicable\0A                         (EXPERTS only) [*]\0A  --bv-intro-pow2        introduce bitvector powers of two as a preprocessing\0A                         pass (EXPERTS only) [*]\0A  --bv-propagate         use bit-vector propagation in the bit-blaster (EXPERTS\0A                         only) [*]\0A  --bv-rw-extend-eq      enable additional rewrites over zero/sign extend over\0A                         equalities with constants (useful on\0A                         BV/2017-Preiner-scholl-smt08) (EXPERTS only) [*]\0A  --bv-sat-solver=MODE   choose which sat solver to use, see\0A                         --bv-sat-solver=help\0A  --bv-solver=MODE       choose bit-vector solver, see --bv-solver=help\0A  --bv-to-bool           lift bit-vectors of size 1 to booleans when possible\0A                         [*]\0A\0AFrom the Datatypes Theory module:\0A  --cdt-bisimilar        do bisimilarity check for co-datatypes (EXPERTS only)\0A                         [*]\0A  --datatypes-exp        enables reasoning about codatatypes (EXPERTS only) [*]\0A  --dt-binary-split      do binary splits for datatype constructor types\0A                         (EXPERTS only) [*]\0A  --dt-blast-splits      when applicable, blast splitting lemmas for all\0A                         variables at once (EXPERTS only) [*]\0A  --dt-cyclic            do cyclicity check for datatypes (EXPERTS only) [*]\0A  --dt-infer-as-lemmas   always send lemmas out instead of making internal\0A                         inferences (EXPERTS only) [*]\0A  --dt-nested-rec        allow nested recursion in datatype definitions (EXPERTS\0A                         only) [*]\0A  --dt-polite-optimize   turn on optimization for polite combination (EXPERTS\0A                         only) [*]\0A  --dt-share-sel         internally use shared selectors across multiple\0A                         constructors [*]\0A  --sygus-abort-size=N   tells enumerative sygus to only consider solutions up\0A                         to term size N (-1 == no limit, default)\0A  --sygus-fair=MODE      if and how to apply fairness for sygus\0A  --sygus-fair-max       use max instead of sum for multi-function sygus\0A                         conjectures (EXPERTS only) [*]\0A  --sygus-rewriter=MODE  if and how to apply rewriting for sygus symmetry\0A                         breaking\0A  --sygus-simple-sym-break=MODE\0A                         if and how to apply simple symmetry breaking based on\0A                         the grammar for smart enumeration\0A  --sygus-sym-break-lazy lazily add symmetry breaking lemmas for terms (EXPERTS\0A                         only) [*]\0A  --sygus-sym-break-pbe  sygus symmetry breaking lemmas based on pbe conjectures\0A                         [*]\0A  --sygus-sym-break-rlv  add relevancy conditions to symmetry breaking lemmas\0A                         (EXPERTS only) [*]\0A\0AFrom the Decision Heuristics module:\0A  --jh-rlv-order         maintain activity-based ordering for decision\0A                         justification heuristic (EXPERTS only) [*]\0A  --jh-skolem=MODE       policy for when to satisfy skolem definitions in\0A                         justification heuristic (EXPERTS only)\0A  --jh-skolem-rlv=MODE   policy for when to consider skolem definitions relevant\0A                         in justification heuristic (EXPERTS only)\0A\0AFrom the Expression module:\0A  --type-checking        type check expressions (EXPERTS only) [*]\0A  --wf-checking          check that terms passed to API methods are well formed\0A                         (default false for text interface) (EXPERTS only) [*]\0A\0AFrom the Finite Field Theory module:\0A  --ff                   enables the finite field solver in applicable logics\0A                         (EXPERTS only) [*]\0A  --ff-bitsum            parse bitsums (EXPERTS only) [*]\0A  --ff-elim-disjunctive-bit\0A                         rewrite disjunctive bit constraints (or (= x 1) (= x\0A                         0)) as (= (* x x) x) (EXPERTS only) [*]\0A  --ff-field-polys       include field polynomials in Groebner basis\0A                         computation; don't do this (EXPERTS only) [*]\0A  --ff-solver=MODE       which field solver (default: 'gb'; see\0A                         --ff-solver=help) (EXPERTS only)\0A  --ff-trace-gb          use a traced groebner basis engine (EXPERTS only) [*]\0A\0AFrom the Floating-Point module:\0A  --fp                   enables the floating point theory in applicable logics\0A                         (EXPERTS only) [*]\0A  --fp-exp               Allow floating-point sorts of all sizes, rather than\0A                         only Float32 (8/24) or Float64 (11/53) (experimental)\0A                         (EXPERTS only) [*]\0A  --fp-lazy-wb           Enable lazier word-blasting (on preNotifyFact instead\0A                         of registerTerm) (EXPERTS only) [*]\0A\0AFrom the Driver module:\0A  --dump-difficulty      dump the difficulty measure after every res